CPI Inflation Analysis Using Microsoft Excel
Project Overview

The Consumer Price Index (CPI) is one of the most important economic indicators used to measure inflation and changes in the cost of living. This project analyzes India's CPI data using Microsoft Excel to identify inflation trends, understand category-wise contributions, examine the impact of COVID-19 on inflation, and explore the relationship between crude oil prices and CPI.

The analysis demonstrates how Excel can be used for data cleaning, trend analysis, Pivot Tables, data visualization, and dashboard development to generate meaningful business insights.

Business Problem

Inflation directly affects consumers, businesses, and government policies. Understanding the factors driving inflation helps policymakers make informed decisions regarding monetary policy, pricing strategies, and economic planning.

This case study aims to analyze India's CPI data and identify the major factors contributing to inflation during the selected period.

