Business Questions
Question 1 – Contribution of Categories to Inflation
Objective

Identify the major categories contributing to India's CPI inflation.

Analysis

Category-wise CPI values were analyzed using Pivot Tables and visualized through charts to determine the relative contribution of each category.

Key Insight

The analysis highlights the categories that contributed the most to inflation during the selected period, helping identify sectors that require greater policy attention.

Question 2 – Year-over-Year Inflation Analysis
Objective

Analyze the Year-over-Year movement of CPI inflation.

Analysis

Year-wise CPI values were compared using Pivot Tables and Line Charts to identify long-term inflation trends.

Key Insight

The analysis reveals how inflation has changed across different years, highlighting periods of higher and lower inflation.

Question 3 – Food Inflation Analysis
Objective

Study the trend in food inflation over time.

Analysis

Food-related CPI indices were examined using Pivot Tables and trend charts to understand changes in food prices.

Key Insight

Food inflation experienced noticeable fluctuations during the analysis period, reflecting changes in food supply, seasonal demand, and market conditions.

Question 4 – COVID-19 Impact on Inflation
Objective

Compare inflation before and after the COVID-19 pandemic.

Analysis

The dataset was divided into pre-COVID and post-COVID periods to compare inflation patterns using charts and summary statistics.

Key Insight

The analysis indicates a significant change in inflation patterns after the COVID-19 pandemic due to supply chain disruptions and changing consumer demand.

Question 5 – Crude Oil Price vs CPI Analysis
Objective

Analyze the relationship between crude oil prices and CPI inflation.

Analysis

Crude oil price trends were compared with CPI trends using line charts to identify possible relationships.

Key Insight

The comparison suggests that changes in crude oil prices may influence inflation by affecting transportation, manufacturing, and logistics costs.

